{"content_hash": "141f8e20255b28a4", "version_id": 553, "article_id": 56, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize", "title_zh": "加拿大诗人安妮·卡森拿下诺贝尔文学奖", "has_translation": true, "topic": "culture", "source": "bbc_culture", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq4g1j54nepyo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1586859411132-573998709aa9?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8Ym9sZCUyMGludmVudGl2ZSUyMGNhbmFkaWFufGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE2NzgxOTd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Isabel Piñeiro on Unsplash", "author": "Isabel Piñeiro", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@isabelpinheiro?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/red-and-white-flag-on-rock-formation-near-body-of-water-during-daytime-MJFBzRgEqEc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(250, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(288, 46%, 48%)", "label": "CULTURE", "seed": "45e27dcc686b"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 194, "reading_minutes": 1.0, "lead": "Anne Carson, a Canadian poet, has won this year's Nobel Prize in Literature. The judges praised her bold and inventive writing, which mixes poetry with old Greek stories.", "lead_zh": "加拿大诗人安妮·卡森获得了今年的诺贝尔文学奖。评委称赞她大胆而富有创意的写作，把诗歌和古希腊故事融合在一起。", "preview": "Carson is 76 years old, and her work often crosses the lines between poetry, fiction and scholarship. The Nobel committee said she won becau", "preview_zh": "卡森今年76岁，她的作品常常跨越诗歌、小说和学术的界限。诺贝尔奖委员会说，她获奖是因为她大胆而富有创意的写作，为现代文学创造了新的形式。听到消息时，她开玩笑说评委选她是“疯了”。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 541, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/56/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 74.737, "size_bytes": 452304, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 220, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/553.json", "paragraphs": ["Carson is 76 years old, and her work often crosses the lines between poetry, fiction and scholarship. The Nobel committee said she won because her bold and inventive writing has created new forms for modern literature. When she heard the news, she joked that the judges were \"crazy\" for choosing her.", "The Nobel Prize honours a writer's whole life of work, and it is seen as the most important award in world literature. The winner receives 12 million Swedish kronor, which is about £900,000. Carson was born in Toronto in 1950, and she has lived in Michigan for many years.", "Her famous works include The Glass Essay and Autobiography of Red. She has taught classics for over 30 years, so Greek literature often inspires her writing. Although her poems are playful and ironic, they move between old and modern styles, and between different types of art.", "Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney called her win a proud moment for Canada. He said her wit, imagination and unique style have brought ancient stories to new audiences. Carson is staying in Iceland at the moment, where she was listening to the wind when she got the call."], "paragraphs_zh": ["卡森今年76岁，她的作品常常跨越诗歌、小说和学术的界限。诺贝尔奖委员会说，她获奖是因为她大胆而富有创意的写作，为现代文学创造了新的形式。听到消息时，她开玩笑说评委选她是“疯了”。", "诺贝尔奖表彰一位作家一生的创作，被视为世界文学中最重要的奖项。获奖者能拿到1200万瑞典克朗，约合90万英镑。卡森1950年出生于多伦多，多年来一直住在密歇根。", "她的著名作品包括《玻璃随笔》和《红色自传》。她教古典学超过30年，所以希腊文学常常给她的写作带来灵感。虽然她的诗俏皮又带讽刺，却在古典和现代风格之间、在不同艺术类型之间自由穿梭。", "加拿大总理马克·卡尼称她的获奖是加拿大的骄傲时刻。他说她的机智、想象力和独特风格把古老的故事带给了新读者。卡森目前待在冰岛，接到电话时她正在听风的声音。"], "body": "Carson is 76 years old, and her work often crosses the lines between poetry, fiction and scholarship. The Nobel committee said she won because her bold and inventive writing has created new forms for modern literature. When she heard the news, she joked that the judges were \"crazy\" for choosing her.\n\nThe Nobel Prize honours a writer's whole life of work, and it is seen as the most important award in world literature. The winner receives 12 million Swedish kronor, which is about £900,000. Carson was born in Toronto in 1950, and she has lived in Michigan for many years.\n\nHer famous works include The Glass Essay and Autobiography of Red. She has taught classics for over 30 years, so Greek literature often inspires her writing. Although her poems are playful and ironic, they move between old and modern styles, and between different types of art.\n\nCanadian Prime Minister Mark Carney called her win a proud moment for Canada. He said her wit, imagination and unique style have brought ancient stories to new audiences. Carson is staying in Iceland at the moment, where she was listening to the wind when she got the call.", "body_zh": "卡森今年76岁，她的作品常常跨越诗歌、小说和学术的界限。诺贝尔奖委员会说，她获奖是因为她大胆而富有创意的写作，为现代文学创造了新的形式。听到消息时，她开玩笑说评委选她是“疯了”。\n\n诺贝尔奖表彰一位作家一生的创作，被视为世界文学中最重要的奖项。获奖者能拿到1200万瑞典克朗，约合90万英镑。卡森1950年出生于多伦多，多年来一直住在密歇根。\n\n她的著名作品包括《玻璃随笔》和《红色自传》。她教古典学超过30年，所以希腊文学常常给她的写作带来灵感。虽然她的诗俏皮又带讽刺，却在古典和现代风格之间、在不同艺术类型之间自由穿梭。\n\n加拿大总理马克·卡尼称她的获奖是加拿大的骄傲时刻。他说她的机智、想象力和独特风格把古老的故事带给了新读者。卡森目前待在冰岛，接到电话时她正在听风的声音。", "text": "Carson is 76 years old, and her work often crosses the lines between poetry, fiction and scholarship. The Nobel committee said she won because her bold and inventive writing has created new forms for modern literature. When she heard the news, she joked that the judges were \"crazy\" for choosing her. The Nobel Prize honours a writer's whole life of work, and it is seen as the most important award in world literature. The winner receives 12 million Swedish kronor, which is about £900,000. Carson was born in Toronto in 1950, and she has lived in Michigan for many years. Her famous works include The Glass Essay and Autobiography of Red. She has taught classics for over 30 years, so Greek literature often inspires her writing. Although her poems are playful and ironic, they move between old and modern styles, and between different types of art. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney called her win a proud moment for Canada. He said her wit, imagination and unique style have brought ancient stories to new audiences. Carson is staying in Iceland at the moment, where she was listening to the wind when she got the call.", "vocab": [{"word": "inventive", "pos": "adj", "zh": "有创意的", "note": "形容人或有新想法的事物", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "scholarship", "pos": "noun", "zh": "学术研究", "note": "不可数，指学术工作", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "honour", "pos": "verb", "zh": "表彰，授予荣誉", "note": "英式拼写，美式为 honor", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "prestigious", "pos": "adj", "zh": "有声望的", "note": "常用来形容奖项或学校", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "classics", "pos": "noun", "zh": "古典学", "note": "指古希腊罗马文学文化研究", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "inspire", "pos": "verb", "zh": "启发，给灵感", "note": "常用 inspire sb to do sth", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "ironic", "pos": "adj", "zh": "讽刺的", "note": "形容说话或作品带反讽意味", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "genre", "pos": "noun", "zh": "体裁，类型", "note": "如小说、诗歌等文学类型", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "audience", "pos": "noun", "zh": "观众，读者", "note": "可指读者群", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "unique", "pos": "adj", "zh": "独特的", "note": "强调与众不同", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "'Bold and inventive' Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize", "summary_original": "Carson, 76, is celebrated for works that often cross boundaries between poetry, fiction and scholarship.", "body_original": "'Bold and inventive' Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize\nBy\nIan Youngs\nCulture reporter\nPublished\n8 October 2026\nCanadian poet, essayist and translator Anne Carson has been awarded this year's Nobel Prize in Literature.\nCarson, 76, is celebrated for works that often cross the boundaries between poetry, fiction and scholarship.\nThe Nobel Prize committee said they had selected her \"for her bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature\".\nCarson responded by joking that the judges were \"crazy\" for honouring her. \"I think they're all crazy... Well, you know, it's crazy,\" she told public broadcaster RUV in Iceland, where she is currently staying.\nThe Nobel Prize is awarded for a lifetime's body of work and is regarded as the most prestigious award in global literature, with the winner receiving 12 million Swedish kronor (£900,000, $1.2m).\nIngrid Carlberg, permanent secretary of the Swedish Academy, said she had broken the news to Carson on the phone shortly before the public announcement.\n\"She had time to tell me was that she is, for the moment, in Iceland, where she is listening to the wind,\" Carlberg, said.\n\"She was taken by surprise but very happy. I could hear that in her voice.\"\nBorn in Toronto in 1950, Carson lives in Michigan and has also held Icelandic citizenship since 2022.\nAnders Olsson, chairman of the Swedish Academy's Nobel committee for Literature, praised the way Carson has \"broken away from lyrical poetry bound to the narrative self and inspired new forms of contemporary literature\".\n\"This method of writing leads to playful and ironic works that move not only between classical and modern poetry but also between different genres and artforms,\" he said.\nCanadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said Carson's win was \"an extraordinary achievement and a proud moment for Canada\".\nThe writer's works feature \"wit, imagination, and a style entirely her own,\" Carney wrote on social media.\n\"She has brought ancient stories to new audiences and transformed the way we think about literature.\"\n'Outstanding importance'\nCarson's notable works include The Glass Essay, Autobiography of Red: A Novel in Verse, Nox, Float and The Beauty of the Husband: A Fictional Essay in 29 Tangos.\nIn 2019, her performance piece Norma Jeane Baker of Troy drew a line between famous beauties from different historical periouds - Helen of Troy and Marilyn Monroe.\nIn 2021, she released The Trojan Women: A Comic, a graphic retelling of Euripides' ancient story; and her translation of Elektra by Sophocles was staged starring Brie Larson in London last year.\nShe has been a professor of classics for more than 30 years and her writing is often inspired by Greek literature.\nHer translations have often given a contemporary twist to ancient works.\n\"Her collaborations with visual artists and choreographers and with opera and theatre directors demonstrate the freedom with which she relates to literary expectations and rule systems,\" Olsson said.\n\"It is this that lies behind the outstanding importance her work since the 1990s has had for the international art and literature scene.\"\nRelated topics\nBooks\nLiterature\nNobel Prize\nMore on this story\nHungarian author László Krasznahorkai wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n9 October 2025\nSouth Korea's Han Kang wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n10 October 2024\nNorway's Jon Fosse wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n5 October 2023", "fetched_at": "2026-10-11T00:23:16.183990", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Carson", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.575, "sm": 100, "em": 575, "cs": 0, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "is", "s": 0.588, "e": 0.7, "sm": 587, "em": 700, "cs": 7, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "76", "s": 0.713, "e": 0.96, "sm": 712, "em": 960, "cs": 10, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "years", "s": 0.96, "e": 1.579, "sm": 960, "em": 1578, "cs": 13, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "old", "s": 1.579, "e": 1.95, "sm": 1578, "em": 1950, "cs": 19, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": ",", "s": 1.95, "e": 2.35, "sm": 1950, "em": 2350, "cs": 22, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "and", "s": 2.35, "e": 2.475, "sm": 2350, "em": 2475, "cs": 24, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "her", "s": 2.487, "e": 2.637, "sm": 2487, "em": 2637, "cs": 28, "ce": 31, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "work", "s": 